(Plan 290: `Append ch to line.` where `ch` is a `text` variable must
compile AND append ch's actual runtime string content onto line - the
analyzer previously rejected this with "Buffer append requires a
buffer source: ch" even though codegen/runtime already handled a
VarType::String identifier correctly via the same path `{ch}` format
interpolation into a buffer already uses.)

a buffer called line is 256 bytes in size.
a text called ch is "hello".
Append ch to line.
Print line.

(A second append proves this really appends onto existing content,
not just writes without erroring)
a text called tail is " world".
Append tail to line.
Print line.

(Text produced dynamically via a format string, not a bare literal,
to rule out any literal/constant-folding shortcut hiding a runtime bug)
a number called n is 1.
a text called digit is "{n add 2}".
Append digit to line.
Print line.

(Same source kind appended into a growable, non-fixed buffer target)
Create a buffer called dyn.
a text called word is "grow".
Append word to dyn.
Print dyn.
